        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "109ab0c3-3076-562c-b5e5-61fe5dcbf450",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hal B. Wallis, Humphrey Bogart\n- Roles: film producer, screen actor, stage actor\n- Companies: Warner Bros.\n- Films: Casablanca, True Grit, The Maltese Falcon, The Big Sleep\n- Concepts: film noir, cultural icon\n\nFacts:\n- Hal B. Wallis, born Aaron Blum Wolowicz on October 19, 1898, was an American film producer.\n- Humphrey Bogart, born on December 25, 1899, was an American screen and stage actor.\n- Hal B. Wallis produced many major films for Warner Bros. featuring stars including Humphrey Bogart, Bette Davis, and Errol Flynn.\n- Humphrey Bogart became a cultural icon for his performances in 1940s film noir movies such as The Maltese Falcon, Casablanca, and The Big Sleep.\n- Hal B. Wallis is best remembered for producing Casablanca in 1942 and True Grit in 1969.\n- Humphrey Bogart died on January 14, 1957.\n- Hal B. Wallis died on October 5, 1986.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
